# All-player Custom Plan browsing

Add an All option to the Custom Plan selector and identify each visible plan by its owner colour.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] The Custom tab selector adds a circular All option divided into slices representing the six player colours.
- [ ] Selecting All displays saved custom plans belonging to every player.
- [ ] Each custom plan row shows a small ownership dot matching its `PlayerColor` beside the plan name.
- [ ] Selecting an individual colour continues to show only that player's plans and statistics.
- [ ] The Default tab retains individual-player behavior and does not offer All unless separately specified.
- [ ] New Plan remains available in All mode.
- [ ] Creating from All opens SCR-004 with Red selected by default.
- [ ] The editor offers only the six individual colours; changing colour before Save assigns the plan to that player.
- [ ] If the untouched generated default name changes owner, it is recomputed from that owner's same-kind plans; a user-edited name is preserved.
- [ ] After Save, the All list shows the plan with the correct ownership dot and individual filtering shows it only for its owner.
- [ ] Switching between All and individual colours preserves custom plans and table scroll integrity.
- [ ] Domain/filtering and UI regression coverage compile for all six players.
- [ ] Focused UI checks pass on a functioning simulator.

## Scope notes

- The All choice is Plan Browser presentation state, not a seventh `PlayerColor`, and must not be serialized as an owner.
- Default naming is calculated from Red when creation begins in All mode and follows the per-owner rules in TASK-022 if the owner changes before the generated name is edited.
